<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1479">1479</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Complete Annals of Đại Việt, Dai Viet su ky toan thu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư, the &quot;Complete Annals of Đại Việt&quot;, is the official national chronicle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, written in classical Chinese. Compiled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-si-lien">Ngô Sĩ Liên</a> and completed in 1479 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-thanh-tong">Lê Thánh Tông</a>, it was extended by later historians and printed in 1697. It is the main source for Vietnamese history up to the 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dai-viet-su-ky-toan-thu.jpg" alt="Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư" width="316" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Nguyễn Thanh Quang at Vietnamese Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DaiVietSuKyToanThu.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
